-- title:
--   Level Γ_H(M) structures on y²+y=x³ in characteristic two
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $2$ with decidable equality, let $w \in L^\times$ satisfy $w^3 = 1$ and $w \neq 1$, let $M$ be a nonzero natural number with $M \neq 0$ in $L$, and let $H \leq (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ be a subgroup. Work with the affine Weierstrass curve $W : y^2 + y = x^3$ over $L$, given by the coefficient tuple $(a_1,a_2,a_3,a_4,a_6) = (0,0,1,0,0)$, and let $\mathcal{X}$ be the type of subsets $s$ of $W(L)$ for which there is a point $P$ of exact additive order $M$ with $s = \{\,u_{\mathrm{val}} \cdot P : u \in H \sqcup \langle -1\rangle\,\}$, where $H \sqcup \langle -1 \rangle \leq (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ is the subgroup generated by $H$ and $-1$ and $u_{\mathrm{val}}$ denotes the canonical natural-number representative of $u$. Write $\Gamma_H(M) \leq \mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb{Z})$ for the subgroup of matrices in $\Gamma_0(M)$ whose image under the homomorphism $\Gamma_0(M) \to (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ (lower-right entry mod $M$, with inverse the upper-left entry) lies in $H$. The assertion is threefold. First, $\#\mathcal{X}$ equals the index of the subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb{Z})$ generated by $\Gamma_H(M)$ and $-1$. Second, there is a surjection $c$ from $\mathcal{X}$ onto the double coset space $\Gamma_H(M) \backslash \mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb{Z}) / \langle ST \rangle$ such that $c(s) = c(s')$ holds if and only if for some $k \in \mathbb{N}$ every $T \in s$ has some $T' \in s'$ with the image of $T$ under the inverse point map of the $k$-th power of the variable change $(u,r,s,t) = (w,0,0,0)$ heterogeneously equal to $T'$. Third, the same holds with $\langle ST \rangle$ replaced by $\langle S \rangle$ and the variable change $(w,0,0,0)$ replaced by $(1,1,1,w)$. Here $S$ and $T$ are the standard generators of $\mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb{Z})$.
--
--   This identifies, for the supersingular curve $y^2+y=x^3$ in characteristic $2$, the set of $\Gamma_H(M)$-level structures up to sign with the fibre of the modular curve $X_H(M)$ above the relevant point, and identifies the orbits on it of the order-$3$ and order-$4$ automorphisms $[\omega]$ and $[i]$ with the double coset spaces $\Gamma_H(M)\backslash\mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb{Z})/\langle ST\rangle$ and $\Gamma_H(M)\backslash\mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb{Z})/\langle S\rangle$. It feeds the computation of ramification and order data for $q$-expansions at level $\Gamma_H$ in characteristic $2$, via [`ModularCurve.ord_census_qExpFunctionFieldC_gammaH_of_char_two`](thm.html#ModularCurve.ord_census_qExpFunctionFieldC_gammaH_of_char_two).
